            {
                "entry_id": "4f34e3bd-e0b5-3692-aba3-ebf1b3f33d24",
                "word": "anodyn",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5cf40483-0750-463b-9b3c-f4e01847de7a",
                        "entry_id": "4f34e3bd-e0b5-3692-aba3-ebf1b3f33d24",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "anodyns"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3eae37c3-b285-30f3-87f4-03903254680b",
                        "entry_id": "4f34e3bd-e0b5-3692-aba3-ebf1b3f33d24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Remède qui calme la douleur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53ae45b9-85e4-4c89-9dca-6fd97fef457f",
                                "sense_id": "3eae37c3-b285-30f3-87f4-03903254680b",
                                "text": "A doses moyennes l’opium est à la fois un anodyn, un hypocinétique et un hyperhémiant ; en d’autres termes, il calme la douleur et apaise les convulsions en même temps qu’il excite la calorification et entretient les forces."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aaa246fe-0f24-4a99-828a-07f3f95d22cd",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f34e3bd-e0b5-3692-aba3-ebf1b3f33d24",
                        "source_sense_id": "3eae37c3-b285-30f3-87f4-03903254680b",
                        "target_lang_word": "anodyne",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anodyne",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2dc83067-418e-3e56-b609-620ed272c042",
                                        "entry_id": "ff8aa6aa-d552-3ed1-946c-47ebf8c9dcbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of soothing or eliminating pain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de282077-4b56-4950-ab3a-5cc666dd2115",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc83067-418e-3e56-b609-620ed272c042",
                                                "text": "Many a time has the vapor of ether been inhaled for the relief of oppressed lungs; many a time has the sought relief been thus obtained; and just so many times has the discovery of the wonderful anodyne properties of this gas, as affecting all bodily suffering, been brushed past and overlooked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74e8d158-9119-4170-964b-38b5aa9eb416",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc83067-418e-3e56-b609-620ed272c042",
                                                "text": "The citrate is the most efficient as an alkali, but irritates some stomachs, the liquor the most anodyne, the acetate the most diuretic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cad1624-3bc1-318b-b7d0-51ceee53a22c",
                                        "entry_id": "ff8aa6aa-d552-3ed1-946c-47ebf8c9dcbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Soothing or relaxing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c746652c-4251-4eb4-9bda-67f4da6f7869",
                                                "sense_id": "2cad1624-3bc1-318b-b7d0-51ceee53a22c",
                                                "text": "Classical music is rather anodyne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f7745210-1de6-33a9-8fcf-5bb8dfd78076",
                                        "entry_id": "ff8aa6aa-d552-3ed1-946c-47ebf8c9dcbc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Noncontentious, blandly agreeable, unlikely to cause offence or debate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9c90999-a497-4d05-90c1-b39b277e26d8",
                                                "sense_id": "f7745210-1de6-33a9-8fcf-5bb8dfd78076",
                                                "text": "It all became so routine, so anodyne, so dull."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "adcc71df-5441-4628-af12-aa74849f9228",
                                                "sense_id": "f7745210-1de6-33a9-8fcf-5bb8dfd78076",
                                                "text": "States typically like to stick to anodyne messages, like saving wildflowers or animals. But every so often a controversy crops up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "393aed23-0eed-48ad-a988-1189c2d87388",
                                                "sense_id": "f7745210-1de6-33a9-8fcf-5bb8dfd78076",
                                                "text": "The Vatican supports the vision of an independent Palestine living in peace alongside Israel, and Francis on Saturday called for a “just solution” to the conflict – the sort of neutral, anodyne language he is expected to adhere to during the stay."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "anodyne",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3439a57c-f8ba-3590-9cbb-ba61b65dd1a0",
                                        "entry_id": "f4d5437a-7ed3-3830-96bd-88138ca5475f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any medicine or other agent that relieves pain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51000ae5-ca0d-3be3-9536-5a36d455c280",
                                        "entry_id": "f4d5437a-7ed3-3830-96bd-88138ca5475f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A source of relaxation or comfort."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7f63b4d-31d8-4798-9e4c-72de187970eb",
                                                "sense_id": "51000ae5-ca0d-3be3-9536-5a36d455c280",
                                                "text": "Nor do I mean to say that Virtue is not Virtue because it is never tempted to go astray; only that dulness is a much finer gift than we give it credit for being; and that some people are very lucky whom Nature has endowed with a good store of that great anodyne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d45e1d6a-5822-443a-877b-1109036f5910",
                                                "sense_id": "51000ae5-ca0d-3be3-9536-5a36d455c280",
                                                "text": "The air was heavy with the perfume of the flowers, and their beauty seemed to bring him an anodyne for his pain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1329c8eb-2c9a-46e1-aa52-ffbcb698b74e",
                                                "sense_id": "51000ae5-ca0d-3be3-9536-5a36d455c280",
                                                "text": "So, with a sigh, because novels so often provide an anodyne and not an antidote, glide one into torpid slumbers instead of rousing one with a burning brand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
